#v(1em)

Dear Michael,

I am applying for the Senior Platform Engineer position in BDC Cloud Services and Customer Enablement. The role is listed at T3 and I want to be transparent that I would be joining at T1.

What draws me to this role specifically is the mix of platform engineering and customer work. I chose to study Business Informatics rather than pure computer science precisely because I wanted to stay close to that boundary between technology and the people using it. Bridging the gap between development teams and customers is something I find genuinely interesting, not a compromise.

On the technical side, I have hands-on experience with SAP BTP and cloud application development from my rotations at SAP. I am comfortable working across teams and in international settings, and I bring a strong foundation in software engineering with TypeScript, Python, and cloud tooling.

I finish my dual studies at DHBW Mannheim in September 2026 and hold an unconditional hire recommendation from SAP. I would be glad to talk through what I could contribute from day one and where I would grow into the role.

#v(2em)

Best regards,

#v(0.5em)

*Max Meinel*
